# netsurf: content blocking in the Vita's resolver
# Generated 2026-09-24
#
# README §14.5: on the Vita every extra origin costs a software TLS
# handshake (~1 s each, hardware run 11), so ad and tracker hosts are
# refused before any lookup or connection. vita/resolve.c checks each host,
# and every domain it is under, against the bundled list
# (app0:/res/blocklist.txt, 71 ad-serving and tracking hosts, narrowed so
# no company's own site is blocked) and the user's
# ux0:data/VitaBrowser/blocklist.txt ("host" blocks, "@@host" allows; the
# user's entries win). A blocked fetch fails at once as
# CURLE_COULDNT_RESOLVE_HOST (patch 49's failed-lookup path). Counted in
# vita_resolve_blocked (the HUD shows it).
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md §Run 14.

